rows.en:
It's a ring that bleeds, you know?
Nobody would want to get mixed up with that, right?
And so time went by.{p}

She'd been thinking she couldn't stay gloomy and depressed forever, too...
So Ishikawa decided to try taking the ring off.
That ruby ring held too many memories.{p}

And then... it wouldn't come off.
The ring wouldn't budge from her finger.
And from the ruby ring, tears of blood again...{p}

Of course she wasn't going to give up, right?
After that, she went to Mr. Miyama every day and kept begging him to give the ring back.
But Mr. Miyama wouldn't listen at all.{p}

The ruby ring was sitting on the balcony!
There was no doubt it was the one Ogura had given her.
Because both their initials were engraved on the inside of the band.{p}

Yoko and I were both dumbfounded.
With this kind of thing, the mood is everything, isn't it?
We'd worked so hard to build up our fear and curiosity, and she blew it all away in one go.{p}

Sanae didn't care about any of that and kept on climbing.
"...Eleven, twelve, thirteen, fourteen. Huh? There are fourteen steps."
That's what she said...{p}

Yoko was a little bit miffed.
"No fair, Sanae, going on ahead all by yourself!"
"Then I'll wait, so hurry up and come on up."{p}

One step... two steps... three steps...
It's actually pretty nerve-racking, you know.
But then,{p}
